# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Cloudflare ignores netlify.toml, so the rules that lived there have to exist
# here too or they vanish silently on deploy. `_headers` needs no translation —
# both hosts read the same file.
#
# Two rules from netlify.toml are deliberately absent. `/app` and `/app/` need no
# rule here: Cloudflare redirects a directory to its trailing-slash form and
# serves index.html from it, which is what the relative asset base needs. And the
# 404 blocks on /builder and /legacy are replaced by simply not uploading either
# — see scripts/deploy.sh, which assembles the site from a file list rather than
# publishing the repository root.

/index            /       301
/editor.html      /app/   301
/editor           /app/   301

# Belt and braces: if a deploy ever does include the repository root, these keep
# the TypeScript source and the superseded prototype from being browsable.
/builder/*        /       301
/legacy/*         /       301
